-- KAN-392 — the 184 duplicate pairs the operator confirmed after the first
-- full Portugal OSM import (run 084e3511-abbd-43a2-9aed-d6a5e16c95d6).
--
-- Found by comparing all 307 per-scope rename reports: of 27,460 flagged
-- pairs, 265 had identical single-token identities once category words and
-- articles were stripped, and 184 of those were within 20 m. Every one was
-- reviewed and confirmed — 182 distinct OSM elements, 0.24% of the import.
--
-- Survivor rule: keep the Foursquare row, hide the OSM element. The
-- Foursquare name is already in the database and its record carries the
-- store attributes, so retaining it changes nothing else about the venue.
--
-- Recorded as a correction rather than a delete, per KAN-386: a later
-- Foursquare reload cannot reintroduce what review has retired, and the
-- decision stays auditable. The importer reads the same registry, so these
-- elements are not re-admitted by a future OSM supplement either.
--
-- Where an OSM element matched two Foursquare rows, both names are listed:
-- those are Foursquare-internal duplicates, which this migration does not
-- address. See KAN-390.
ON CONFLICT(source, source_id) DO UPDATE SET
  visible = excluded.visible,
  name_override = excluded.name_override,
  dedupe_name_override = excluded.dedupe_name_override,
  review_note = excluded.review_note;
